# Eval/test build artifacts (2026-10-13) — large compiled binaries, do not commit.
orchestrator_go_linux
orchestrator_eval_plannerfix_*

# Live test runtime data (CaSKG graph, spawner outputs) — generated at runtime.
tests/live/data/

# --- Tracked-bloat gaps closed 2026-10-18 (extension rules *.exe/etc. missed these) ---
# Dependency directories — never commit
frontend/node_modules/
bridge/node_modules/
# Build output
frontend/dist/
# Extensionless Go binary + suffix variant (*.exe matches neither)
/orchestrator_go
*.exe.old
# One-off root analysis dumps / scripts
/_*.txt
/gen_large_test.py
# Backup residue
*.bak
# Secrets — real API keys (ONION_ARCHITECTURE.md §6: NEVER EXPORT)
/.env
/config.json
/config_windows.json
# MCP config can embed real API keys (e.g. video-mcp.json GEMINI/GROQ) — local only.
/workspace/mcps/video-mcp.json

# Nested-repo backup (2026-10-18): inner .git was neutralized so the outer
# workspace monorepo governs this directory. Kept on disk, must not be tracked.
/.git_inner_backup_*/

# ExperienceStore runtime data (JIT learning artifacts): decision precedents,
# routing matrix, role profiles, task patterns, skill affinity, etc. These are
# generated at runtime by orchestrator (e.g. embeddings in decision_precedents.json
# can be 768-dim × thousands of entries) and change on every task run. Should
# never be committed — causes git blame noise, multi-instance conflicts, and
# repo bloat. Only seed.json is source-controlled.
experience/*.json
!experience/seed.json

# workspace/skills — flat .json skill definitions (imported from directory
# skills, carry runtime staged_at metadata written by PendingSkills staging,
# config/types.go:247) and directory skills (SKILL.md, imported via
# external_skill_adapter.go). Both are runtime-derived/imported content that
# changes on every skill import/load; the loader reads them from disk at
# runtime (config/loader.go:301-317, os.ReadDir + *.json) regardless of git
# tracking. Kept on disk, must not be tracked.
workspace/skills/

# workspace/sops — imported offensive-security SOPs (ext_offensive_*.json),
# generated one-per-skill when an external multi-step skill is imported via
# external_skill_adapter.go:117-126 (body containing "## " or "1." auto-
# registers as a SOP). These are import-derived, not canonical seeds: the
# built-in SOPs (seed_builtins.go builtinSOPs) remain tracked. Gitignoring
# keeps import-generated offensive content out of the repo while preserving
# the canonical SOP set.
workspace/sops/ext_offensive_*.json
